      "description": "Watch Napoli vs Como highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 30, 2026. The Serie A clash between SSC Napoli and Como delivered a masterclass in tactical discipline and clinical finishing. Both sides entered the fray with high ambitions, creating an atmosphere of anticipation that persisted throughout the encounter. First Half Fireworks The game erupted into life in the 17th minute when Como took a shock lead. Martin Baturina found the back of the net with a precise left-footed strike, set up by Assane Diao following a clever build-up involving Lucas Da Cunha . SSC Napoli responded with determination, and on August 30, 2026, they found their equalizer. Rasmus Hoejlund unleashed a spectacular effort from outside the box, beating the keeper with his left foot after being fed by Amir Rrahmani and Stanislav Lobotka . However, the parity lasted only four minutes. A defensive lapse from Amir Rrahmani in the 34th minute proved costly, as Anastasios Douvikas capitalized on the error. Assisted by the influential Baturina , Douvikas restored Como's lead with a clinical right-footed finish, leaving the home side trailing at the break. Second Half Pressure and VAR Drama As the second half progressed, Napoli ramped up the pressure, introducing Kevin De Bruyne and David Neres to spark a comeback. Despite waves of attacks, the Como defense, marshaled by Jean Butez , remained resolute. Butez made a vital save in the 90th minute to deny a header from Lorenzo Lucca , while Alex Meret at the other end had to stay alert to stop a late attempt from Douvikas . The defining moment arrived deep in stoppage time. In the 95th minute, play was halted for a VAR check regarding a potential Napoli goal. After an agonizing wait, the officials ruled the goal out due to an offside against Lorenzo Lucca . Despite holding 42% possession and throwing everything forward, Napoli couldn't find the breakthrough, as Como held on for a famous victory."
